# Goal 6: Fix pow — p_h adjustment discarded in final computation

## Function
`pow` (double-precision power function)

## Source Files
- C source: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/libm/mathd/powd.c`
- Rust source: `/home/leochanj/Desktop/libmcs/newexp/rust-s4/src/mathd.rs` (line 3504, function `powd`)

## Failure Type
MISMATCH — wrong output

## Symptom
```
C:    pow 0x1p+1 0x1.4p+3 = 0x1p+10
Rust: pow 0x1p+1 0x1.4p+3 = 0x1.b2d809254afbcp+11
```
Input: `pow(2.0, 10.0)`. Expected `1024.0` (`0x1p+10`), Rust gives ~3557.5.

## Root Cause
In the final `2**(p_h+p_l)` computation section (Rust lines 3676-3686), the adjustment `p_h -= t` from C is computed but **discarded**:

**C code (correct):**
```c
if (i > 0x3fe00000) {
    ...
    p_h -= t;   // p_h is modified in place
}
t = p_l + p_h;  // uses adjusted p_h
```

**Rust code (buggy):**
```rust
if i2 > 0x3fe00000 {
    ...
    let mut p_h2 = p_h;
    p_h2 = p_h2 - t_var;
    let _ = p_h2;  // BUG: discards the adjusted value!
}
let mut tt = p_l + p_h;  // uses ORIGINAL p_h, not adjusted
```

The `let _ = p_h2;` explicitly discards the modified value. The subsequent computation on line 3688 uses the original `p_h` instead of `p_h - t_var`, causing a large error in the final result.

## Fix
In `mathd.rs` lines 3676-3688, restructure to propagate the p_h adjustment:

Replace the block starting at line 3676:
```rust
let p_h_adj;
if i2 > 0x3fe00000 {
    n = j + (0x00100000 >> (k + 1));
    let k2 = ((n & 0x7fffffff) >> 20) - 0x3ff;
    let t_bits: u64 = ((n as u64) & !((0x000fffffu64) >> (k2 as u32))) << 32;
    let t_var = f64::from_bits(t_bits);
    n = (((n & 0x000fffff) | 0x00100000) >> (20 - k2)) as i32;
    if j < 0 { n = -n; }
    p_h_adj = p_h - t_var;
} else {
    p_h_adj = p_h;
}

let mut tt = p_l + p_h_adj;
```

## Success Criteria
- `pow 0x1p+1 0x1.4p+3` produces `0x1p+10` (bitwise match with C, i.e. exactly 1024.0)
- All other pow tests continue to pass
- exp2 tests pass (exp2 depends on pow — see Goal 5)
